{44800}{Foreigners are unwelcome in Malicorne, and even the city's own inhabitants are not free to leave.}
{44820}{A woman escaped from Malicorne and now lives somewhere nearby.}
{44840}{The mayor of Malicorne has declared magicians outlaws. His men persecute them even beyond the city walls.}
{44860}{Professor Quentin Blafard disappeared after making a mysterious discovery. His wife suspects that the Malicorne authorities were involved.}
{44880}{They say the soldier stationed at the bridge is rather fond of the bottle...}
{44900}{A man suspected of sorcery is in prison awaiting execution.}
{44920}{The bandit Neril Tenduil is wanted for theft. A reward of 200 coins is offered for his capture, dead or alive. Inquire with the First Sergeant of the city guard.}
{44940}{The mayor recently closed the old mine.}
{44960}{A traveling merchant named Dr. Julius Maximus has set up near the inn. He claims his elixir can cure all manner of fatigue...}
{44980}{Neril Tenduil stole Ernesto Mendego's pendant at the three-tree crossroads south of Malicorne. He was last seen heading for the caves farther south.}
{45000}{Golim Dradoc cannot see a thing without his spectacles. According to the innkeeper, the din of the steam machinery in his workshop must be making him deaf as well.}
{45020}{Ever since the magician Erwin Cornebrume was executed three months ago, no one has been willing to buy his house.}
{45040}{Malicorne's physician told me that the dying half-ogre I encountered suffers from acute Meliotonitis. The remedy is a mushroom called the Trompelamort, which is said to grow in the old mine.}
{45060}{Jacques Trowbridge studies and keeps jars of voracious wood-eating insects called wingless polyopterans. Merely setting their jar on wood excites them enough to escape and devour the wooden surface in minutes!}
{45080}{Golim Dradoc is known to be a man of considerable influence.}
{45100}{By some accounts, Dr. Julius Maximus's Elixir is remarkably effective.}
{45120}{Madam Lil's establishment in Tarant has reportedly closed.}
{45140}{A priest named Dante has reportedly been seen near Malicorne.}
{45160}{Malicorne was built upon the ruins of an ancient city.}
{45180}{My arrival in the city did not go unnoticed.}
{45200}{Malicorne's club is reserved for the city's leading citizens.}
{45220}{Foreigners are unwelcome in Malicorne, and even the city's own inhabitants are not free to leave.}
{45240}{Malicorne's merchants sell their goods to everyone, but they refuse to buy anything from a foreigner.}
{45260}{As long as the bridge provides a route outside Malicorne, the mayor will keep the old mine closed, for it too leads beyond the city's borders.}
{45280}{The ingredients needed to cast Erwin Cornebrume's spell�a vial of dragon's blood and a vial of elven spring water�are said to lie within the old mine.}
{45300}{The magician Erwin Cornebrume was imprisoned and executed one week before the day I traveled into the past.}
{45320}{Several passages have collapsed in the old mine. It is closed until further notice.}
{45340}{Some say the hotel manager and Irina Petroff are having an affair.}
{44901}{The guard arrested a magician within the city itself! He was plotting against the mayor!}
{44921}{A reward of 200 coins is offered to anyone who brings back the bandit Neril Tenduil, dead or alive.}
{44941}{The mayor has closed the old mine. No one is permitted to approach it.}
{44961}{A traveling merchant has parked his wagon behind the inn. He supposedly sells an elixir for every sort of fatigue. A charlatan, if you ask me...}
{45001}{Do you know Golim Dradoc? They call him Squinty Golim because he cannot see a thing without his spectacles! They say he even wears them to bed! And he must be going deaf from the din of all that steam machinery. If he ever left his workshop, one could break into his chest without being heard�the noise would cover everything!}
{45021}{Ever since the magician Erwin Cornebrume was executed three months ago, no one has been willing to buy his house. People seem wary of the place...}
{45081}{Do you know Golim Dradoc? They say his influence reaches far... That must come in terribly handy when he needs to scratch his backside...}
{45101}{Ever since I tried Dr. Julius Maximus's Elixir, my migraines have vanished! That doctor is a saint!}
{45121}{They say Madam Lil's establishment in Tarant has closed!...}
{45141}{Long ago, I met a priest named Dante at the Sour Barnacle in Black Root. They say he has recently been seen in these parts...}
{45161}{Did you know that Malicorne was built upon the ruins of an ancient city? Entrances to tunnels can still be found here and there, leading to old, partially collapsed cellars.}
{45181}{A suspicious individual reportedly arrived in the city not long ago. An illegal entrant, no doubt. Someone rather like you...}
{45201}{[He looks you over contemptuously.] This club declines further every day. They truly will admit anyone now...}
{45241}{Malicorne's merchants conduct trade only with local residents. If you are not from here, they will gladly sell you their goods, but they will never buy anything from you...}
{45301}{Erwin Cornebrume was executed for sorcery a week ago. Yet he belonged to Malicorne's old nobility and was a pure-blooded human!...}
{45321}{Several passages have collapsed in the old mine. It is closed until further notice.}
{28000}{}
{21881}{If you're travelling the hills northwest of Stillwater, watch out for old Drog Blacktooth, the ogre.  He's mostly harmless, but you never know with ogres...}
{24080}{Rumor has it that Mr. Merton Vorman had a bastard, half-ogre son.  He's purportedly buried behind the Vorman Manor, in the family mausoleum.}
{24081}{Have you heard the rumors about Merton Vorman?  It’s said that the mausoleum behind his house holds his bastard, half-ogre son!}
{24100}{Rumor has it that something strange has happened in Ter'elon, an elven village located in the Erriwind Forest to the north.  Qin'ar, the leader of the village, has come to Vormantown to speak with Merton Vorman.}
{24101}{Word has come down from the Erriwind Forest…something strange has happened in the elven village of Ter'elon!  Qin’ar, their leader, has come here to speak with Merton Vorman!}
{24120}{Rumor has it that Veryk Ironwill, the king of the Stone Heart Clan, has come to Vormantown.  No one seems to know why.}
{24121}{Did you see who came into town?  Veryk Ironwill, the king of the Stone Heart Clan!  Word has it he’s staying up at Merton Vorman’s mansion, but no one knows why he’s here!}
{24140}{Rumor has it that Mr. Shackleford takes care of all of Mr. Vorman's personal affairs.}
{24141}{Have you met Mr. Shackleford?  He's Mr. Vorman's lawyer, and takes care of all of his personal affairs.  He's quite an individual!}
{24160}{Rumor has it that Merton K. Vorman founded Vormantown as some sort of "social experiment".}
{24161}{Mr. Vorman founded Vormantown almost 10 years ago...he called it a "social experiment", I think, but I don't know much about things like that...}
{24200}{Strange beasts have been seen wandering the local woods and caves.  The townspeople think it is a sign of Minra's evil.}
{24201}{Have you heard of the strange beasts?  All different forms have been seen wandering the woods and caves of late.  It is a sure sign that Minra's evil is spreading!}
{24220}{The town of Stillglade has a deadly curse upon it.}
{24221}{Steer clear of the town of Stillglade in your travels, stranger.  An evil witch cursed the town many years ago and the entire town died a slow and painful death.  It is said the curse remains to this day.}
{24240}{Kallen is a powerful necromancer that the townspeople say I should avoid.}
{24241}{Have you come across Kallen in your travels?  Quite a powerful necromancer, he is...  But what a twisted sense about him!  Watch out for that one, if you value your sanity!}
{24260}{I should be wary of groups of Minra's soldiers along the main roads.}
{24261}{Groups of Minra's soldiers have been spotted along the main roads.  Stay out of their way, if you know what's good for you.}
{24280}{The evil and powerful witch Minra has imprisoned the queen and taken over the throne in the capital city of Tyr.}
{24281}{Have you heard about the evils taking place in Tyr, the capital city?  Our queen has been imprisoned by the powerful witch Minra.  I have heard that evil began to spread like a plague the moment Minra took the throne!}
{44580}{I just learned of a Cattanese halfling legend about a spider-demon called Merow Vortahm. The story goes that it is able to cloud your mind and make you believe it's actually a beautiful human woman. Posing as a woman who is lost, it comes to an isolated farm, sizes up the available food supply, then finds a dark place close by to lay her eggs. Her offspring have the same ability to charm people and have no trouble overwhelming the farm. It's just a legend, of course.}
{44600}{There's a large necropolis just north of Monaco on Cattan.}
{44620}{The island of Cattan was known as Kai'tan's Abode in ancient times. An interesting bit of trivia.}
{44640}{The Plainwicke Plantation has an infestation of magickal creatures known as Merow Vortahm. The creatures are trapped on a river island, but that won't last much longer.}
{44680}{Merow Vortahm is not the last of her kind on Cattan.}
{24060}{There seems to be a haunted hunting lodge just up the road from Lynchbany. It could be a good base of operations in this area.}
{24061}{There seems to be a haunted hunting lodge just up the road from Lynchbany. It could be a good base of operations in this area.}
{40000}{I encountered a strange old man on the outskirts of Shrouded Hills}
{40020}{The book "Horror Among the Dark Elves" recounts the hair-raising experience of Mr. Renford A. Terwilliger and his capture and escape from the Dark Elven Village of T'sen-Ang.  On a side note, the dedication reads..."To sweet Raven, who still haunts my memory."}
{40040}{I found a book in the grave of Victor Misk, but its binding was most obviously a fake.  The actual book contained within it is "How Nasrudin Defeated the Nefarious Arronax! and Other Stories" by Oscar Grant.  There is a printer's seal on the title page.  It reads "Roseborogh Gift Shop".}
{40060}{The crypt of Nasrudin held a skeleton dressed in robes, which I noticed was missing its right finger.}
{40080}{The message in the crypt led me to an ancient vault.  Within was the journal of Saint Mannox, which described his betrayal by an elf named K'an Hua, as well as the true function of the Panarii church.  The vault also held his family sword, engraved with the name 'Mannox'.}
{40100}{The book in the grave of Phillip Misk is an actual copy of "Horror Among the Dark Elves."  Within it is a map which pin-points the location of the Dark Elf village.}
{40120}{I found a purchase order for a signet ring.  The order was made by a Benjamin Bates, but the ring was purchased for his son, Gilbert Bates.}
{40140}{I found a receipt for goods purchased from P. Schuyler & Sons in Ristezze's file cabinet.  The address is in the city of Tarant.}
{40160}{The note to Loghaire Thunder Stone from an elf named M'in Gorad states in no uncertain terms the desired sentence for the dwarves of the Black Mountain Clan--exile to the Isle of Despair.  The note seems to have been sent from the elven village of Qintarra.}
{40180}{The note from Gunther Wilhelm describes the differences between an old copy of the Archaeon and the current one.  It seems that Gunther believes that the final resting place of Nasrudin is not Caladon, but the Island of Thanatos.}
{40200}{I found a love note from a man named Renford A. Terwilliger to Raven.  It seems they were very close.  He also mentioned something about his search for the Dark Elves.}
{40220}{On the inside lid of the sarcophagus was a cryptic message which seemed to be painted in blood.  There was an illustration of a broken ring with an 'X' within, as well as two words in a tongue unknown to me.}
{40240}{A strange shrine at the crash site had this carved into it:  "And His spirit will be reborn on wings of fire in hills shrouded in fog. Archaeon 5:16"}
{40260}{It seems as if only I have survived the crash of the I.F.S. Zephyr. The zeppelin was unexpectedly set upon by strange flying machines. Among the wreckage I found a dying gnome who gave me a signet ring and bid me to find the boy who owned it, with a vague warning of something that "is almost here". He also said that he had "escaped", but I have no clues as to where he escaped from.}
{40280}{I have identified the dead gnome as Preston Radcliffe, from the ticket he had in his pocket.}
{40300}{Buried underneath the wreckage of one of the bizarre flying machines responsible for downing the Zephyr, I have located a dead Ogre. Unbelievably, he seems to have been the pilot of the craft. I also found an amulet bearing an eye within a hexagram on his person.}
{40320}{Preston Radcliffe was not a gnome, but a dwarf named Stennar Rock Cutter. For some unknown reason, he did the unthinkable - he cut off his beard simply to pass as a gnome. He must have starved himself as well to make himself appear more gnomish.}
{40340}{Gilbert Bates, the industrialist, seemed to feel some need to unburden his conscience by telling me his deepest secret. He developed his first steam engine from a Black Mountain Clan dwarven prototype which he improved upon. He did not invent it, as everyone had assumed. He feels this youthful indiscretion of his led to the disappearance of the Black Mountain Clan somehow, and is anxious to find out what really happened to them. He was warned by mysterious robed figures in the night to never speak of his association with the Black Mountainers, or the fact that he used their engine to develop his own.}
{40360}{Gilbert Bates has sent me to Ashbury to look up a sea captain named Edward Teach, an "associate" of Bates that handles "special" jobs for him. He sounds like some sort of pirate, to me. He is meant to ferry me to the Isle of Despair, a penal colony.}
{40380}{Gilbert Bates has had an attempt made on his life by an assassin wearing the sign of the Molochean Hand, the eye in the hexagram. The Molochean Hand was an order of assassins 500 years ago, and they are thought to have long since disappeared. Bates was not certain whether the would be assassin was a true servant of the Molochean Hand or not.}
{40400}{I was attacked by someone wearing an amulet bearing the eye in the hexagram symbol, similar to the one that I found on the Ogre in the wreckage of the flying machine.}
{40420}{I was attacked by someone wearing an amulet bearing the image of an eye within a hexagram.}
{40440}{I found Gudmund Ore Bender, a crazed dwarf hiding in the bowels of the Black Mountain Clan mines, babbling incoherently about the Wheel Clan being pawns of the elves. He hid himself to keep from being banished with the rest of his clan, and I think guilt has caused his rampant paranoia. He has trapped many of the mine's tunnels to prevent "them" from "getting" him.}
{40460}{The Pillar of Truth within the Black Mountain Clan's mines tells the story of their banishment to the Isle of Despair for allowing technology to spread to the humans, principally because of Gilbert Bates and his steam engine. Strangely, it seems elves were there to effect the banishment, with the cooperation of the Wheel Clan.}
{40480}{Ogdin, Thorvald's door guard, has told me I need to fight in the pit to gain an audience with him. I need to search out Gorrin the pit master to arrange a bout for me.}
{40500}{There is only one dwarf on the Isle of Despair, and he seems to be in charge. His name is Thorvald.}
{40520}{Thorvald says he is the only dwarf who has ever lived on the Isle of Despair. The Black Mountain Clan were never there.}
{40540}{Thorvald has informed me that I will need a special pair of spectacles, constructed of thin slices of Kathorn crystal, to be able to see the entrance to the mines of the Wheel Clan.}
{40560}{Stanley Xavier Hippington has given me a small trap and a bottle of "Stillwater Giant Scent" to use in my attempt to capture the giant. He has instructed me to take off any armor I may be wearing (to lessen any noise I may make, as well as to make me appear less threatening) and use the scent on my body before approaching it. I am then to use the trap to capture the giant in its resting form, that of a blue rabbit.}
{40580}{I am to take the caged Stillwater Giant to Dr. Tristan Fenwick, of the Zoological society in Tarant to authenticate it.}
{40600}{Upon questioning him of the strange signet ring, Constable Owens told me that Ristezze the Importer might have further information about its origins.}
{40620}{Ristezze the Importer told me that P. Schuyler & Sons is located at 44 Devonshire Way in the city of Tarant, and marked my map accordingly.}
{40640}{I met a dwarf named Magnus loitering outside of P. Schuyler & Sons.  He had some strange theories about their business practices.}
{40660}{Magnus and I have decided to cooperate while investigating P. Schuyler & Sons.  It seems that he's come across a bracelet that purportedly comes from his lost clan.}
{40680}{I found an ancient dwarven tomb deep beneath P. Schuyler & Sons.  I believe they are using its resources for their business.}
{40700}{I found the three Schuyler brothers-Winston, Niles and Edward-on the lowest level of the dwarven tomb.  Theirs is an old family of Necromancers who use their powers to locate valuable and rare items.}
{40720}{I agreed to keep silent about the business operations of P. Schuyler & Sons in return for the identity of the owner of the signet ring.}
{40740}{I agreed to keep silent about the business operations of P. Schuyler & Sons in return for the identity of the owner of the signet ring.  Unfortunately, Magnus was unhappy about it, and was lost in the ensuing battle.}
{40760}{Pelonious Schuyler, the long-dead father of the Winston and his brothers, was called back from the dead in order to answer my question about the ring.  He rambled incoherently for a few moments and then divulged the owner's name-a Mr. Gilbert Bates.}
{40780}{I met a sea captain named Edward Teach.  He told me his ship was for hire, but only through permission of Gilbert Bates.}
{40800}{Edward Teach told me the story of how he came to own his boat, the Gypsy Shadow.  The Gypsy's former owner, a man named Jack Skellybones, was supposedly murdered by the ghost of Stringy Pete, who, according to Teach, was the meanest pirate to have ever sailed the seas of Arcanum.  I found the story entertaining, if not a bit fanciful.}
{40820}{I met Randver, the son of Loghaire Thunder Stone.  It seems that Loghaire has gone into exile and that Randver is King-in-Waiting of the Wheel Clan.}
{40840}{Randver told me the elves had something to do with the banishment of the Black Mountain Clan.  Unfortunately, he doesn't know the exact nature of their involvement, and that Loghaire went into self-exile soon after the banishment.}
{40860}{Randver told me that Loghaire disappeared into the caverns of the Dredge, an old system of dwarven mines that now houses an assortment of foul creatures.}
{40880}{Randver told me of the Shape and the Stone, a form of dwarven philosophy.  It seems that Loghaire may have exiled himself in response to a perceived betrayal of this code.}
{40900}{Randver showed me a secret passage that he uses in order to see his father.}
{40920}{Loghaire Thunder Stone told of a delegation of elves, supposedly sent from the Silver Lady, who visited him not long after the invention of the first steam engine.  The elves were outraged at the use of technology in the destruction of their forests, and demanded retribution.}
{40940}{Loghaire told me that the elves threatened war if the Black Mountain Clan was not punished, and the elves demanded to be the party responsible for their banishment to the Isle of Despair.  I found this strange, considering the elves are not a war-like people.}
{40960}{Loghaire agreed to the terms of the elves because he feared the enormity of a conflict between the elves and the dwarves.}
{40980}{I convinced Logahire that his Stone was still true, and that his rightful place was back among his people.}
{41000}{Loghaire told me the name of the elf who led the delegation-M'in Gorad.  He said to begin my search for this M'in Gorad in the ancient elven village of Qintarra, and that someone in Stillwater might know of Qintarra's exact location.  He also told me to return if I find out what really happened to the Black Mountain Clan.}
{41020}{Loghaire, despondent and lost after the news of the Black Mountain Clan, gave me a note and told me continue my search in the elven village of Qintarra.  He said that someone in Stillwater might know of its location.}
{41040}{I met Raven, daughter of the Silver Lady.  I told her I needed to speak with her mother, but it seems I must remove some humans from Falcon's Ache before this is possible.  Falcon's Ache is elven holy ground on the edge of the Glimmering Forest.   Under no circumstances am I shed blood while removing these men.}
{41060}{I told Raven about all that has transpired.  She knew not the name of M'in Gorad, but told me to speak with the Silver Lady concerning these things, and to return to her once I had.}
{41080}{I spoke with Raven concerning the visions of the Silver Lady.  Much of what we talked about was speculation, but it seems that M'in Gorad might be a Dark Elf.}
{41100}{Raven told me that I need to find an individual named Renford A. Terwilliger.  It seems this Terwilliger was a researcher who was searching for the Dark Elves.  Raven believes that if anyone would know where their village is located, he would.}
{41120}{Raven told me that I need to seek further answers about Nasrudin in the city of Caladon.  There I will find the First Temple of the Panarii, whose priests are well-versed in the history concerning the banishment of Arronax.}
{41140}{I spoke with the Silver Lady, and asked her about M'in Gorad.  She had many visions, all of which were cryptic and unclear.}
{41160}{In light of the recent discoveries about the involvement of the Dark Elves in the banishment of the Black Mountain Clan, I asked the Silver Lady what I should do next.  She told me that my answers lie with Nasrudin.}
{41180}{Alexander, First Acolyte of the Panarii, told me that the remains of Nasrudin are located beneath the Panarii Temple.}
{41200}{Alexander told me that I need to speak with Gunther Willhelm, the church historian, and Hadrian, the church archaeologist, concerning the remains of Nasrudin.}
{41220}{Alexander, First Acolyte of the Panarii, has discovered that I am the sole blimp crash survivor.  He seemed overjoyed to make my acquaintance, hailing me as the Living One, but warned me that the High Priest was not a believer.  It seems he has issued a church-wide order to denounce me as a fraud.  Quite strange, concerning he's never met me.}
{41240}{Alexander told me to be careful about whom I told about being the blimp crash survivor.  He said Gunther Willhelm would accept me, but that Hadrian might not.  I'll have to be careful in dealing with them.}
{41260}{Alexander told me of Saint Mannox, a sacred figure in the Panarii Church.}
{41280}{Alexander told me of the ascension of Saint Mannox.  Supposedly, Nasrudin took Mannox directly from this plane of existence to the next-the only time in the history of the church this has happened.}
{41300}{Alexander showed me where I might see a copy of the Archaeon, the holiest book in the religion of the Panarii.}
{41320}{I told Alexander of what I discovered concerning the murder of Mannox by K'an Hua.  He was none too happy.}
{41340}{I spoke with Gunther Willhelm, the church historian.  He told me of some translations he is working on...an older and previously undiscovered copy of the Archaeon.  He found an interesting discrepancy in the meaning of the name "Panarii".}
{41360}{I confided in Gunther Willhelm about the blimp crash.  He accepted me heartily, and told me he'd help in any way he could.}
{41380}{Gunther Willhelm told me that Alexander is a direct descendant of  Saint Mannox.}
{41400}{I found it strange that the person who witnessed the ascension was the same person who discovered the remains.  The name of the individual was K'an Hua.}
{41420}{Gunther Willhelm told me to use caution in revealing myself to Hadrian the Archaeologist, but that he would be the best source of information concerning the remains of Nasrudin.}
{41440}{Gunther told me the meaning of the words on the inside of the crypt.  The first word means "opposite", the second means "truth".  He knew not the meaning of the broken ring.}
{41460}{It seems Gunther has found another discrepancy in the older translation of the Archaeon.  This has led him to conclude that the remains of Nasrudin are not here,  but on the Isle of Thanatos.}
{41480}{I told Gunther Willhelm of my discovery of the journal of Mannox.  He told me I should tell Alexander as soon as possible.}
{41500}{I spoke with Hadrian the Archaeologist about the remains of Nasrudin.  It seems that even he does not have access to them.}
{41520}{Hadrian gave me a tip on how I might get in to see the remains of Nasrudin.  He said to take a look around in the local sewers.}
{41540}{After a little subterfuge, Hadrian confided in me that he's discovered a way to see the remains of Nasrudin first-hand.  I am to enter the old catacombs through the a crack in the sewer walls, directly under the temple.  According to Hadrian, there is a secret door that leads directly to the burial chamber.  It is magically sealed, and the password to open it is "Crimstone".}
{41560}{I told Hadrian of the blimp crash, but he became angry and didn't want to speak with me anymore.}
{41580}{I brought back the skull I found in the tomb of Nasrudin, and showed it to Hadrian.  It seems that the skull is human, and not elven.  Hadrian is visibly upset by the discovery.}
{41600}{I told Hadrian of the message written in blood on the lid of the sarcophagus.  He doesn't know what it means, but told me to consult Gunther Willhelm about it.}
{41620}{I told Hadrian of what I've discovered about the murder of Saint Mannox.  He told me I need to speak with Alexander about it immediately.}
{41640}{I discovered Edward Teach in the Sour Barnacle in Black Root while seeking passage to the Isle of Thanatos.  He told me that he'd lost the Gypsy Shadow in a game of chance to a man named Killian Drake.}
{41660}{Edward Teach suggested three options for obtaining passage to the Isle of Thanatos-winning the Gypsy back from Killian Drake, buying a boat for myself, or attempting to steal a boat from the ghost of Stringy Pete.}
{41680}{I met an old Drunk in the Sour Barnacle in Black Root.  He had a map to the secret cove of Stringy Pete.  It may warrant further investigation.}
{41700}{I found the secret cove of Stringy Pete, where his remains are buried.}
{41720}{I confronted the ghost of Stringy Pete about getting his boat.  It seems he is cursed to sail the seas of Arcanum for all of time.}
{41740}{Stringy Pete thinks there may be a way to break his curse.  If I do what is necessary, he will give me his boat.}
{41760}{I confronted Kerghan the terrible in his fortress.  He told me the story of his banishment from Arcanum by the Elven Council because of the necromantic experiments he'd been conducting.}
{41780}{Kerghan seems to have grown in power during his stay in the Void.  It seems that time does not pass here.}
{41800}{Kerghan sees all life as an abomination, a deviation from the natural order.  He wants to get rid of all life, both in the Void and in Arcanum.  Only then, he says, will the tormented souls of the dead have peace.}
{41820}{I spoke with the widow of Victor Misk.  She said that he was acting strangely in his last days.  It seems that his behavior was brought about by the recent release of the book  "The Curse of T'sen-Ang", which named him as the owner of the last remaining copy of "T'sen-Ang: Horror Among the Dark Elves".}
{41840}{It seems that Victor Misk died only days before my arrival.  He is buried at the Caladon Cemetery.}
{41860}{The widow Misk has no idea who revealed the secret of her husband's ownership of the rare book.  This may warrant further investigation.}
{41880}{I asked the widow Misk what significance the town of Roseborough, or its Gift Shop, might have to her.  She said none, except that Victor's father, Phillip Misk, is buried in the Roseborough cemetery.}
{41900}{I met an old dwarf named Bingham Shulefest at the Caladon Cemetery who claimed he knew Magnus.  Magnus denied it, but was defensive upon further questioning.}
{41920}{Bingham Shulefest was an agent of the Molochean Hand.  Magnus has little to say about the matter.}
{41940}{The woman at the Hall of Records said that Renford Terwilliger was dead, but that he had written a book called "T'sen-Ang: Horror Among the Dark Elves."  She said I might be able a copy of the book at the city library in Tarant.}
{41960}{The Librarian in Tarant said that "T'sen-Ang: Horror Among the Dark Elves" is extremely rare, and that no copy is available.  She did give me a book called "The Curse of T'sen-Ang", which was very recently released.}
{41980}{"The Curse of T'sen-Ang" is a book about the strange set of circumstances surrounding Renford A. Terwilliger and his book "...Horror Among the Dark Elves".  It also reveals the only surviving owner of the book-a man named Victor Misk, who lives in Caladon.}
{42000}{I spoke with Raven concerning M'in Gorad, who it seems might be a Dark Elf.}
{42020}{I told Hadrian that I noticed the skeleton in the sarcophagus was missing its right finger.  He thinks that it may be Saint Mannox who was buried there, and not Nasrudin.  Needless to say, he is very upset.}
{42040}{Dr. Tristan Fenwick has informed me in no uncertain terms that the Stillwater Giant is a hoax. The blue rabbit I had trapped as the Stillwater Giant was simply a normal rabbit painted blue.}
{42060}{Dr. Fenwick has told me that showman H.T. Parnell has a fake Stillwater Giant pelt on display.}
{42080}{M'in Gorad has told me that the dark elves were waiting for years to find an excuse to banish a group of dwarves to the Void, for the purpose of constructing a gate to enable Arronax to return.}
{42100}{M'in Gorad divulged that Stennar was able to escape through the minimally functioning gate because of his lack of magickal aptitude.}
{42120}{I have joined with the dark elves, and M'in Gorad has told me to go to the Panarii temple in Caladon to meet with K'an Hua, the high priest.}
{42140}{I have retrieved a note from someone named K'an Hua addressed to M'in Gorad. It infers that the BMC are in the Void, and Stennar somehow escaped from there using an unfinished gate that the dwarves are constructing. It sounds as if the dwarves are being used as slave labor to construct a means for Arronax to return. The note also refers to Vendigroth and their attempt to retrieve some sort of device.}
{42160}{K'an Hua has confided in me that the dark elves have taken over the Panarii religion to subvert it and to create doubt in people's minds as to whether Arronax actually existed.}
{42180}{K'an Hua let slip that his secrets lie with Nasrudin, but I could not persuade him to elaborate when I pressed the issue.}
{42200}{K'an Hua has told me that the Panarii religion, under his subversive guidance, has ceased maintaining the wards that keep the rift between Arcanum and the Void sealed. Without regular maintenance, the wards are becoming weakened.}
{42220}{I have found out that Arronax was Nasrudin's son.}
{42240}{K'an Hua told me the tale of Arronax's banishment. Vendigroth had begun building a device to kill Arronax when he had asked them to cease their dangerous and irresponsible experimentation with technology, so he was forced to destroy them in self-defense. Arronax was then forced to go to war with the Elven Council, and if he had not been failed by his weak allies, he would have been victorious. Even alone, his strength was such that the struggle to banish him created a rift between Arcanum and the Void that needed to be sealed with magickal wards.}
{42260}{I heard the saga of Kerghan the Terrible, the only human member of the Elven Council. When he discovered the necromantic arts, the Council asked him to do no more research into them, as they felt that they had enormous potential for evil. When Arronax discovered Kerghan had been toying with people's spirits, he persuaded the council to sentence him to banishment. He went meekly, without a fight, even though he possessed enormous power.}
{42280}{I was told the story behind the banishment of the Bane of Kree. He was a nomad warrior who was able to gather together nearly all the ancient nomadic tribes and create a vicious army out of them. When his army descended on Kree, he mercilessly killed every man, woman and child that lived there. Nasrudin was forced to confront him and banish him single handedly. This was the beginning of Nasrudin's reputation which eventually led him to near mythical status in the eyes of all Arcanum.}
{42300}{I was told the story of the banishment of Kraka-tur, a conniving, twisted monster, half-man and half-dragon, who terrorized cities and villages, killing their inhabitants and burning them to the ground.  After a colossal battle, he was subdued and banished.}
{42320}{I was told the story of the banishment of Gorgoth, who was a mindless beast with an insatiable appetite.  He was finally captured by the Council after a struggle which lasted for days, and, with no other alternative, it was decided that he be banished from Arcanum.}
{42340}{Nasrudin is still alive! I located him on Thanatos and he told me the true story behind the legend of Arronax's banishment. Arronax had destroyed the town of Vendigroth when they tried to create a device to combat him. Nasrudin led the battle to banish his own son for his crimes, and the resulting war devastated both their armies. After banishing Arronax, Nasrudin and his allies created Magickal wards to keep Arronax from returning from the Void.}
{42360}{I have heard that the Vendigroth device was designed to drain a mage of his life force while he is cocooned in his impenetrable regenerative shell.}
{42380}{Arronax has told me that he has been imprisoned by Kerghan for nearly two thousand years.}
{42400}{The dark elves have been misled by Kerghan into believing he is Arronax, so that they would help return him to Arcanum.}
{42420}{Arronax has suggested that I gain an audience with Kerghan to prove to me that he is insane and that Arronax is telling me the truth.}
{42440}{Arronax has asked me to release him so that he may join me in the fight against Kerghan. He does not know how the magickal shield he is trapped within is being maintained, however.}
{42460}{Unused}
{42480}{Arronax has told me that it would be wise to recruit more help before confronting Kerghan.}
{42500}{I will need to deduce the proper use of the portals to navigate my way around the Void successfully.}
{42520}{After I dragged myself from the wreckage of the zeppelin crash, I was approached by a monk of the Panarii religion. He seems to believe that I am the "Living One", the reincarnation of some deity of theirs.}
{42540}{The "Living One" is meant to be the reincarnation of an Elf named Nasrudin, a powerful elf wizard.}
{42560}{I received a note from a strange man at the Wellington Gentleman's club in Tarant.  Upon opening it, I found the note contained an address: 57 Mulligan Bone Alley.}
{42580}{I met a strange dwarf today. His name was Jormund, and he lived in Qintarra, of all places. Even stranger is that he claimed to be a mage, trained by an elf! He confided in me that he is terribly unhappy about serving out the rest of his contract under an elf named Wrath.}
{42600}{I met a creature named Kan Kerai.  He is the chieftain of the Melokaan, a race of sentient reptiles who live the Dark Fens.  He is angry...it seems a great wrong has been done against his people.}
{42620}{From speaking with Kan Kerai, I've deduced that his people are being killed for their skins by local poachers.}
{42640}{Upon convincing Kan Kerai that he need not wage war against all of mankind, he offered me the services of one his warriors.  The creature's name is Waromon.}
{42660}{Wrath was killed by poison. I need to speak with Sharpe, the apothecary about who might have purchased the poison from him.}
{42680}{I have found out that Treat was descended from the Black Legion, created by Zalakar during the Age of Legend. This ancestry is what enabled him to transform into a hideous snake creature during our battle.}
{42700}{I need to deduce the method by which Pollock is able to enter and exit his house without being detected, in order to kill him without having to commit to a suicidal frontal assault on his home.}
{42720}{A fellow with a rather strong stench told me to speak with Muggs, a well dressed dwarf I saw in a bar in the Boil, if I was interested in joining the Clan Maug.}
{42740}{Upon entrance to the caverns of the Stonecutter Clan I was set upon by zombies, much to my surprise. It seems one Erland Iron Heart had discovered an ancient necromancer's laboratory off the caverns of the Clan and inadvertently created a number of undead through a scientific method he devised.}
{42760}{I met a man named Edward Willoughsby, who claimed he was the Chairman of the Tarantian Industrial Council.  After a short conversation, he invited me to visit his offices, in the City Hall of Tarant.}
{42780}{Edward Willoughsby mentioned some "personal" measures he was taking to control crime in the Boil.  He told me to look up a man named Sebastian at Caleb Malloy's in the Boil if I was interested in assisting in the endeavor.}
{42800}{Edward Willoughsby appointed me the mediator between Tarant and Caladon in the negotiations concerning Caladon's membership into the United Kingdom.  He told me to travel to Caladon and meet a man named Renard in front of the Royal castle.  Renard is to counsel me further concerning the negotiations once I've arrived.}
{42820}{Chief Inspector Henderson wishes for me to make haste in my attempt to stop the Whytechurch demon L'anamelach. If I tarry too extensively, the king's advisors will call in one Franklin Payne, a well known big game hunter, to hunt the demon down.}
{42840}{Heinrich Jenks has contracted me to kill King Farad of Caladon.  Because of my special privileges as mediator of the negotiations, I am to enter the royal castle, find the kitchens and speak with a man named Vernon.  He will instruct me further.}
{42860}{Heinrich Jenks has contracted you to kill King Farad of Caladon.  If you receive an appointment from Edward Willoughsby as mediator of the negotiations between Tarant and Caladon, you are to enter the royal castle, find the kitchens and speak to man named Vernon.  He will instruct you further.  Otherwise, you are to speak with a man named Bullors at the Caledonia's docks, and he will get you into the castle where you can then meet Vernon.}
{42880}{Heinrich Jenks has contracted you to kill King Farad of Caladon.  You are to meet a man named Bullors at the Caledonia's docks.  Apparently, this Bullors will sneak you into the castle, where you are to find a man named Vernon in the royal kitchens.  Vernon will instruct you further.}
{42900}{I found two dead men in Elder Joachim's room in Shrouded Hills. They were both wearing an amulet with the sign of the eye in the hexagram on it.}
{42920}{Elder Joachim left Virgil a note, telling us to check the telegraph office in Tarant for a message from him, when we get there.}
{42940}{A bloke named Thaddeus Mynor has offered me membership in the "Thieves Underground" if I steal a map of the sewers underneath Tarant from City Hall and deliver it to him.}
{42960}{After inquiring about Rorry Limes at the Tarantian Hall of Records, I found that he owns a building.  The address is 57 Mulligan Bone Alley.}
{42980}{A telegram from the Elder Joachim said that he was investigating the assassins who seem intent on trying to kill me.  We're to travel to the Bleeding Rose Inn in Stillwater.  Once there, we're to speak with Inn Keeper concerning how to contact Elder Joachim.}
{43000}{The ancient text given to me by Joachim is about the Molochean Hand.  The reason behind their separation from the Derian Ka seems to be something that was discovered about Kerghan, who was the first of the dark necromancers and whose death was the reason behind the formation of the Order of the Dead.}
{43020}{Virgil left me for a moment today in the Caladon Cemetery, and I found him standing in front of the the grave of a Lawrence Brummond.  He told me that Brummond had been a friend of his, and that they had grown up together in Tarant.  This may warrant further investigation if we ever return there.}
{43040}{A woman I met on the streets of Tarant has bade me to come round to her house at 3 Lungsten Road for possible employment.}
{43060}{I met a strange bloke in Tarant today, a bit of a lurker he was. He told me to drop in on a fellow named Thaddeus Mynor that lives on the corner of Westrel South and Quilton Bend. I'm meant to inquire about some sort of Thieves Underground organization.}
{43080}{After speaking with Gilbert Bates about the possible "religious" aspects of what has happened to me, he has suggested I stop by the Panarii temple in Tarant to obtain more information. It is located on the northern end of Lion's Head Circle.}
{43100}{Jorian the Diviner has sent me to look at a mural on the wall of the main hallway before he will let me speak with Simeon Tor, leader of Tulla. He will not tell me the reason for this.}
{43120}{Simeon Tor told me of an old sorcerer named Pelojian, the founder of Tulla. He was also an artist, a poet, and a clairvoyant.}
{43140}{I have been told that Mr. Willoughsby can give me master training in persuasion.  He lives in Tarant.}
{43160}{According to Thaddeus Mynor, now that I am a member of the Thieves Underground I can buy and sell goods at the "fence" on 11 Low Dervish Road, near Devonshire.}
{43180}{Jason C. Guy would like me to let him know if I find any signs of ancient technology in my travels.}
{43200}{I have been told that Sammie White can give me master training in pick pocket.  He can normally be found near Metro Station in Tarant.}
{43220}{If I wish to become a master at prowling, I must locate the master by deciphering the note I received after becoming an expert.}
{43240}{I have been told that Kietzel Pearce can give me master training in bow.  He can be found in Blackroot.}
{43260}{I have been told that Adkin Chambers can give me master training in dodge.  He is a hermit that lives outside of Stillwater.}
{43280}{I have been told that Sir Garrick Stout can give me master training in melee.  He is the captain of the guards in Dernholm.}
{43300}{I have been told that Clarissa Shalmo can give me master training in throwing.  She is a mercenary in Black Root.}
{43320}{I have been told that Doctor Edmund Craig can give me master training in backstab.  However, he fled Tarant to escape murder charges and is in hiding in an unknown location.}
{43340}{I have been told that Frederick T. Fitzgerald can give me master training in spot trap.  He has a room in the Bridesdale Inn in Tarant.}
{43360}{I have been told that Gurin Rockhollow can give me master training in gambling.  He can be found in the gentlemen's club in Tarant.}
{43380}{I have been told that J.M. Morat can give me master training in Haggle.  He can normally be found in a bar in Tarant.}
{43400}{I have been told that Fawn can give me master training in healing.  She can be found in Quintarra.}
{43420}{I have been told that Hieronymous Maxim can give me master training in repair.  He can be found in his factory in Caladon.}
{43440}{I have been told that William Thorndop can give me master training in firearms.  He resides in Ashbury.}
{43460}{I have been told that J.T. Morgan can give me master training in locksmith.  He is currently being held in Caladon's high security prison.}
{43480}{I have been told that Daniel McPherson can give me master training in trap disarming.  He resides in Caladon.}
{43500}{Hieronymous Maxim has told me that if I were to bring him a hunting rifle, a loading mechanism, and a revolver chamber he would construct me a mechanized gun.}
{43520}{I was attacked by a strange man at the crash site.  He was very curious as to what I was doing there, and assaulted me after a few questions.  I'm afraid there is something very odd going on here.}
{43540}{I was approached by a strange man at the crash site, but Virgil confronted him and he ran away.  He seemed overly curious as to why we were there, almost to the point of hostility.  I'm afraid there is something very odd happening here.}
{43560}{I have been told that Expert training for Dodge can be found in Blackroot or Qintarra.}
{43580}{I have been told that Expert training for Melee can be found in Blackroot or on the Isle of Despair.}
{43600}{I have been told that Expert training for Throwing can be found in Dernholm or Ashbury.}
{43620}{I have been told that Expert training for Spot Trap can be found in Blackroot or the Wheel Clan.}
{43640}{I have been told that Expert training for Firearms can be found in Blackroot or Shrouded Hills.}
{43660}{I have been told that Expert training for Locksmith can be found in Caladon or Black Root.}
{43680}{I have been told that Expert training for Disarm Traps can be found in Caladon, Roseborough or possibly at the Wheel Clan.}
{43700}{Lukan the Witless told me about something called the Thieves Underground, and that I might be able to find out more about it in Tarant.}
{43720}{I fooled Lukan into thinking that I was part of the Tarantian chapter of something called the Thieves Underground.  If I ever go there, it might warrant further investigation.}
{43740}{I have found a plaque on one of the flying machines that bore the legend "Maxim Machinery, Caladon".}
{43760}{A Panarii priest told me about Arronax, an evil elf who opposed Nasrudin and the Elven Council during the Age of Legends.  This would appear to be the individual whom I'm supposed to confront in this so-called "final battle."}
{43780}{A Panarii priest told me about Nasrudin, the benevolent leader of the Elven Council who lived during what he called the "Age of Legends".  The Panarii seem to hold this fellow in high regard.  I suppose that's a bit comforting as I'm supposed to be his reincarnation.}
{43800}{A Panarii priest told me about the Archaeon, a sacred book of Nasrudin's teachings which is housed in the First Panarii Temple in the city of Caladon.  This may warrant some further investigation.}
{43820}{Now that I am a member of the Clan Maug, I've been told to look up Mr. Damian Maug himself. He resides in the Bentley, an old hotel at the top of the North Boil.}
{43840}{I found a promissory note from a man named named Elmer Burbottom to Wesley, Lillian Misk's butler.  The note, which promised Wesley 500 coins, was unspecific as to what the payment was for.}
{43860}{After inquiring about Elmer Burbottom at the Hall of Records in Tarant, I was given his address in Ashbury, which is 14 Trellis way.}
{43880}{Upon entering the home Of Elmer Burbottom, I found an assailant who quickly teleported away.  I spoke briefly with Mr. Burbottom before he died.  It seems that Mr. Burbottom wrote "The Curse of T'sen-Ang" under the assumed named of Kendrick Wales.  He also confirmed that he paid Welsey for the information concerning Victor Misk.}
{43900}{Thaddeus Mynor has told me that a Cedric Appleby, who resides at 29 Low Dervish Row, wants something stolen from Gilbert Bates' house.}
{43920}{Thorvald expressed an interest in a bottle of Norian's moonshine in exchange for the information regarding the location of the Wheel Clan.}
{43940}{Madame Toussaude told me that the Garringsburg painting could be found at 57 Mulligan Bone Alley.}
{43960}{I have been told that if I am in need of a good laugh, I should look up a certain Cedric Appleby, residing at 29 Low Dervish Row, and mention Gilbert Bates to him.}
{43980}{I have ascertained that Gilbert Bates lives at 50 East End Avenue, at the end of the Kensington Broadway.}
{44000}{Simeon Tor has told me that Pelojian was a great artist, and that he painted the Mural of Enlightenment. He also told me that his paintings are said to help those who meditate on them become closer to achieving oneness.}
{44020}{Simeon Tor is of the opinion that Pelojian's poetry revealed his inner self, but was difficult to understand. This is speculation, though, as none of Pelojian's original poetry has survived. It is only known through others' writings.}
{44040}{Pelojian is said to have been a great clairvoyant, and his spirit should be able to tell me the location of Vendigroth, even if he had never seen it when he was alive.}
{44060}{No one is certain as to the meaning of the symbol in the center of the Mural of Enlightenment. Some feel it is the symbol of a lost college of Magick.}
{44080}{I'm to go to the Mushroom Inn at 23 King's Way in Caladon to inspect the latest Whytechurch murder scene.}
{44100}{I've been given the task to search the rooms of the Whytechurch murder victims. Their addresses are: 21 Dragon Turnabout (off of Temple Road) and 1 Whytechurch Landing (between Grey Wolf Terrace and Temple Road).}
{44120}{Sarah Toone told me that her mother always wanted the mine to stay within the family.}
{44140}{The new owner of the Bessie Toone Mine is Stanton Importers, located at 25 Lion's Head Circle in Tarant.}
{44160}{After reading the journal of Thorvald Two Stones, I am convinced that the Black Mountain Clan has never been on the Isle of Despair.}
{44180}{Dr. Gershwin wants me to retrieve the skulls of Jin and Xin, the famous Ren'ar siamese twins, from their mausoleum in the Tarant Cemetary.}
{44200}{Percival Toone let it slip that his sister is living in Dernholm.}
{44220}{Arthur Tyron has fled Black Root, as "they" were getting too close. His present whereabouts are unknown.}
{44240}{Gladys, the old lady in that wants me to locate her missing ring, has informed me that a man named Archibald might have some idea about where I may find the ring. He is meant to live near the docks in Dernholm.}
{44260}{I was refused entry into the Wellington Gentlemen's club for obvious reasons.  The doorman told me that if I had an issue with the club rules that I should speak with Mr. Wendell Wellington, the owner of the establishment.  Unfortunately, the doorman wasn't very forthcoming about where I might find the gentleman.}
{44280}{I inquired at the Hall of Records as to the address of Mr. Wendell Wellington.  He lives at 42 Vermillion Road.}
{44300}{I heard what seemed to be a recorded voice from a strange device that I presume was built thousands of years ago by the Iron Clan.  It told me to find the Book of Durin's Truth.}
{44320}{I have been asked by Kietzel Pierce, the Bow Master, to keep an eye out for his lost student, Dudley Crosston.  If I should locate him, I should inform Dudley that Kietzel has gone on to Caladon on the kings business.}
{44340}{King Praetor told me of the sad state of affairs in his kingdom of Cumbria. He blames technology for causing the decline in Cumbria's fortunes.}
{44360}{King Praetor feels that he was misled by his Magickal advisors who had assured him that technology was weak in comparison to Magicks.}
{44380}{There seems to be a haunted hunting lodge just up the road from Lynchbany. It could be a good base of operations in this area - once I get rid of the ghosts, of course.}
{44400}{The entertainers for the Brandybuck fair are late coming to town.}
{44420}{The promoter of the Brandybuck fair is worried the others may have taken a wrong turn and met some bandits. Perhaps I should go help the little fellows out.}
{44440}{Farmer Maggot is extremely protective of his potatoes. I've been advised to give him a wide berth.}
{44460}{Mr. Dakia Foghat is sweet on a traveling-show lass named Leeka Newba. I'm sure he's much too old for her, but who am I to judge if a fellow tries to recapture his youth with a younger woman?}
{44480}{The Shire of Brandybuck has the dual honour of being the largest halfling community and their sheep produce the softest wool in the land.}
{44500}{The town of Leahbo cannot call itself a shire anymore. Something to do with too many "longshanks", the larger races, living there.}
{44520}{Leeka Newba does not like Dakia. She's convinced he's too old for her.}
{44540}{Until this day, I had always assumed the expression "Kill them with kindness" to be just a figure of speach. Today I met a woman named Weqia Rurrae who showed me otherwise. If anyone could do this, it would be her!}
{44560}{There is a small farm for sale in Brandybuck.}
{44660}{The creature known as Merow Vortahm had a very tramatic childhood as a slave to barbarian halflings, which accounts for her psychotic hatred of them.}
{44700}{}
{44720}{A man who lives along the shore of Ivory Lake has informed me that one of the unusual qualities of the lake is that teleportation spells do not work once you leave the shoreline. Curious.}
{44740}{At least one group of Elves have taken offence to other people moving too close to the Glimmering Forest. I need to use caution when I travel through the region.}
{44760}{The town of Marcyona should be getting quite a bit of new business now that a forgotten bridge across the river has been rediscovered.}
{30000}{The belongings of Professor Siegfried were distributed among the people present at his funeral: the antique dealer, the castellan, the gardener. There was a fine helmet, a precious pendant and a pair of valuable gloves.}
{30020}{The Barman hides in the cellar a domestic animal that swallows everything and anything. The people of the mansion are looking for it to hunt it.}
{30040}{The son of Golim the antique dealer is a little rascal. He counterfeited his father's writing to make a fake note addressed to his schoolmaster. He has a real forger talent, according to his father...}
{30060}{According to the manor cook, among the close friends of the wife of the castellan (the gravedigger, the gardener and the bartender), one was often with her. Some half-elf.}
{30080}{According to my companion, the bartender, a man called the Master of Tears seeks the tears of his beloved, Niniel the Gentle.}
